1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:06,409
AegisAgent extends my Memorial University data science capstone into a fraud investigation prototype.

2
00:00:06,409 --> 00:00:13,015
This recording uses the original saved models and public synthetic transactions, with isolated demonstration cases.

3
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:20,980
The dashboard scores the complete development window and keeps the top two hundred threshold-breaching alerts.

4
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:26,850
Changing the selection updates the transaction profile and all three component model scores.

5
00:00:26,850 --> 00:00:32,645
The stacked score is compared with the saved threshold, about zero point seven eight seven.

6
00:00:32,645 --> 00:00:38,650
This is an alert ranking score, not proof of fraud or a reliable individual probability.

7
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:47,500
Creating a case records the transaction, model version, score, actor, and timestamp.

8
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:51,291
I add an assignment rationale and start a human review.

9
00:00:51,291 --> 00:00:57,416
The case now has an owner and a new version, with both transitions visible in its event history.

10
00:00:57,416 --> 00:01:00,242
No regulatory decision has been made.

11
00:01:03,450 --> 00:01:09,025
I attach a model observation through the local evidence utility, then inspect it in the dashboard.

12
00:01:09,025 --> 00:01:13,263
This is recorded model output, not an AI-generated narrative.

13
00:01:13,263 --> 00:01:16,874
The integrity check verifies the linked file and event chain.

14
00:01:16,874 --> 00:01:22,284
These hashes detect ordinary tampering. External audit anchoring remains future work.

15
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:33,692
The retained historical evaluation gave ensemble precision-recall AUC of point seven seven seven in development, dropping to point six seven one on the later tail.

16
00:01:33,692 --> 00:01:37,635
The velocity forest ranked slightly better in both windows.

17
00:01:37,635 --> 00:01:41,020
These are not measurements from the revised training code.

18
00:01:41,020 --> 00:01:46,961
The later tail is not a pristine external test, so independent validation is still needed.

19
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:53,138
All transactions are public synthetic data, not Canadian banking records.

20
00:01:53,138 --> 00:01:57,990
Bedrock drafting and S3 archiving are optional and were not exercised in this recording.

21
00:01:57,990 --> 00:02:03,464
Real institution data, operational security, and institutional approval remain future work.

22
00:02:05,450 --> 00:02:10,446
A traceable path from model alert to human review, with explicit limits.

23
00:02:10,446 --> 00:02:16,006
This is a portfolio prototype, not a production or regulatory compliance claim.